# 🍳 Recipe Search Application

A full-stack Flask application that leverages the Spoonacular API to help users discover, save, and manage recipes with personalized search history.

## 🚀 Live Demo

[View Demo](your-demo-link) | [API Documentation](your-api-docs)

## ✨ Features

- **Smart Recipe Search**: Powered by Spoonacular API with 360,000+ recipes
- **User Authentication**: Secure registration and login system
- **Personalized Dashboard**: Track search history and favorite recipes
- **Detailed Recipe Views**: Ingredients, instructions, nutritional info
- **Account Management**: Password updates and account deletion
- **RESTful API**: Clean endpoints for frontend integration
- **Responsive Design**: Mobile-first approach for all devices

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

- **Backend**: Flask, Flask-SQLAlchemy, Flask-Login
- **Database**: SQLite (dev) / PostgreSQL (production ready)
- **Authentication**: Flask-Login with secure password hashing
- **API Integration**: Spoonacular Recipe API
- **Frontend**: Jinja2 templates, Bootstrap 5
- **Deployment**: Docker ready, Heroku compatible

## 📋 Prerequisites

- Python 3.12+
- Spoonacular API Key ([Get one free](https://spoonacular.com/food-api))
- pip package manager

## 🔧 Installation

1. **Clone the repository**
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/Abdinasir03/recipe-search-app.git
   cd recipe-search-app
Create virtual environment

Copypython -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
Install dependencies

Copypip install -r requirements.txt
Configure environment variables

Create .env file in root directory:

SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key-here
SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI=sqlite:///recipes.db
SPOONACULAR_API_KEY=your-spoonacular-api-key
FLASK_ENV=development
Initialize database

Copyflask db init
flask db migrate -m "Initial migration"
flask db upgrade
Run the application

Copyflask run
Access at http://localhost:5000

📡 API Endpoints
Authentication
POST /api/register - Create new user account
POST /api/login - Authenticate user
POST /api/logout - End user session
Recipes
POST /api/search - Search recipes with query
GET /api/search/<recipe_id> - Get detailed recipe info
GET /api/trending - Get trending recipes
User Management
GET /api/search_history - View search history
DELETE /api/search_history/<item_id> - Remove history item
PUT /api/account - Update account details
DELETE /api/account - Delete user account
🖥️ Usage Examples
Search for Recipes
Copy# POST /api/search
{
    "query": "vegan pasta",
    "cuisine": "italian",
    "diet": "vegan",
    "maxReadyTime": 30
}
Get Recipe Details
Copy# GET /api/search/12345
# Returns detailed recipe with ingredients, instructions, nutrition
🏗️ Project Structure
recipe-search-app/
├── app/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── models.py          # Database models
│   ├── routes.py          # API endpoints
│   ├── auth.py            # Authentication logic
│   └── templates/         # HTML templates
├── migrations/            # Database migrations
├── static/               # CSS, JS, images
├── tests/                # Unit tests
├── requirements.txt      # Dependencies
├── config.py            # App configuration
└── run.py               # Application entry point
🚀 Deployment
Docker
Copydocker build -t recipe-app .
docker run -p 5000:5000 recipe-app
Heroku
Copyheroku create your-app-name
heroku config:set SPOONACULAR_API_KEY=your-key
git push heroku main
🧪 Testing
Copy# Run all tests
pytest

# Run with coverage
pytest --cov=app tests/
